cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Projecting the religious composition of countries: a probabilistic cohort-component model and its out-of-sample evaluation"
authors:
  - family-names: Flick
    given-names: Conrad
version: 0.7.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/FLICK11-hash/religion_world_map_predictor"
abstract: >-
  A probabilistic cohort-component projection of the religious composition of
  200 countries from 2020, by religion, migrant generation and five-year age
  group, driven by fertility, mortality, religious switching and international
  migration, with exact attribution of every change in share to its mechanism.
  The model is evaluated out of sample on historical decades against
  persistence and trend baselines, its interval calibration is measured, and
  its projections are benchmarked against an independent published projection.
  The evaluation finds no variant distinguishable from persistence at decadal
  horizons and intervals several times too narrow, and shows that
  disagreements between data vintages exceed disagreements between models.
keywords:
  - statistics
  - applied statistics
  - statistical demography
  - population projection
  - cohort-component model
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - forecast evaluation
  - interval calibration
  - religious demography
  - religious switching
  - international migration
